WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:07.585 --> 00:00:08.390
Hi!

00:00:08.422 --> 00:00:09.281
I'm Ana.

00:00:09.313 --> 00:00:11.023
Welcome to 'What to Say'!

00:00:31.286 --> 00:00:35.374
Do you know what to say when you meet someone face-to-face for the first time?

00:00:35.444 --> 00:00:39.591
Listen out for useful language for meeting face-to-face.

00:00:39.716 --> 00:00:42.786
Then, we'll practise saying the new phrases –

00:00:42.830 --> 00:00:44.185
after this.

00:00:47.075 --> 00:00:47.899
Hi.

00:00:47.952 --> 00:00:48.952
Hi, Eva.

00:00:49.002 --> 00:00:49.792
How are you?

00:00:49.827 --> 00:00:51.286
I'm very well.

00:00:51.511 --> 00:00:52.821
I love your hair.

00:00:52.865 --> 00:00:54.549
It's fabulous!

00:00:54.584 --> 00:00:55.584
Thanks, Noelia!

00:00:58.365 --> 00:00:59.905
Are you Noelia?

00:01:00.382 --> 00:01:01.302
Vanya?

00:01:01.346 --> 00:01:02.240
Yes!

00:01:02.327 --> 00:01:06.415
Hello! It's so good to finally meet you in person!

00:01:06.485 --> 00:01:07.888
You too!

00:01:08.134 --> 00:01:10.554
It's great to put a face to a name.

00:01:11.075 --> 00:01:13.185
I thought you were in Spain this week.

00:01:13.224 --> 00:01:16.266
I was, but I came back early.

00:01:16.404 --> 00:01:19.712
So, how are you finding it here?

00:01:19.911 --> 00:01:21.608
Fine!

00:01:21.935 --> 00:01:23.144
Really good!

00:01:23.541 --> 00:01:26.088
All the team have been so welcoming.

00:01:26.426 --> 00:01:27.111
Good!

00:01:27.164 --> 00:01:29.307
We have a lovely team here.

00:01:29.760 --> 00:01:33.241
Now, has Emir set you up with an email address?

00:01:33.311 --> 00:01:34.311
He has.

00:01:34.361 --> 00:01:36.557
I'm all ready to go!

00:01:36.766 --> 00:01:37.766
Perfect!

00:01:37.833 --> 00:01:39.967
Is there anything else you need?

00:01:40.064 --> 00:01:42.095
Not right now, thanks.

00:01:42.205 --> 00:01:44.869
Well, let me know if I can help at all.

00:01:44.910 --> 00:01:46.810
I will, thank you.

00:01:47.072 --> 00:01:49.808
Actually, I've got an idea.

00:01:50.292 --> 00:01:52.236
What are you doing later?

00:01:52.449 --> 00:01:54.410
I haven't got any plans.

00:01:54.658 --> 00:01:55.456
Great.

00:01:55.491 --> 00:01:56.993
Meet me here at six.

00:01:57.036 --> 00:01:58.074
Don't be late!

00:02:01.930 --> 00:02:03.979
So what's the plan?

00:02:04.885 --> 00:02:07.877
We're going to see the local area by bike.

00:02:07.997 --> 00:02:10.836
I'll show you all the best coffee shops.

00:02:10.958 --> 00:02:12.096
Cool!

00:02:12.244 --> 00:02:13.244
Let's go!

00:02:16.610 --> 00:02:17.610
Hello again!

00:02:17.793 --> 00:02:21.636
I think Noelia and Vanya are going to get on really well!

00:02:21.847 --> 00:02:27.050
So, did you notice the useful phrases
used for meeting face-to-face?

00:02:27.293 --> 00:02:29.708
Listen to me and then repeat.

00:02:30.136 --> 00:02:33.294
It's so good to finally meet you in person.

00:02:37.775 --> 00:02:40.775
It's so good to finally meet you in person.

00:02:44.892 --> 00:02:47.507
It's great to put a face to a name.

00:02:50.881 --> 00:02:53.585
It's great to put a face to a name.

